[100.666595, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- It brings its own markup, CSS and content elements.\u001b[57GYour\u001b[62Gdesign\u001b[69Gis\u001b[72Gfully\u001b[78Gcustom\u001b[85Gwith\u001b[90GBEM\u001b[94Gclasses,\u001b[103Gso\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gyou'd spend your time overriding it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1m5. Paste the HTML in and switch off TYPO3's page output (\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mconfig.disableAllHeaderCode\u001b[39m).\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m- This is a trap. TYPO3 normally writes the \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m<html>\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m<head>\u001b[39m, CSS and JS includes and meta\u001b[92Gtags.\u001b[98GWith\u001b[103Gthis\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gsw\u001b[8Gtch,\u001b[13Gthe template car\u001b[30Gies the whole document and TYPO3\u001b[63Gadds \u001b[69Gothing, so the meta \u001b[91Ggs and\u001b[98Gevery\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bextension's\u001b[17Gassets are lost.\u001b[34G\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhy option 1\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mThe design maps cleanly onto TYPO3.\u001b[41G\u001b[22mEach\u001b[46Gof\u001b[49Gthe\u001b[53Gfive\u001b[58Glayouts\u001b[66Gbecomes\u001b[74Ga\u001b[76Gpage\u001b[81Glayout\u001b[88Geditors\u001b[96Gcan\u001b[100Gchoose:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mHome\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mSidebarLeft\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mDefault\u001b[39m (full width),\u001b[46G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mSidebarRight\u001b[39m \u001b[60Gnd \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mNarrow\u001b[39m. Each\u001b[76Gneeds \u001b[83G page template wit\u001b[102G a\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bmatching name.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mThe header and footer become partials.\u001b[44G\u001b[22mThese\u001b[50Gare\u001b[54Gfragments\u001b[64Gof\u001b[67Gthe\u001b[71Gbody\u001b[76Gonly.\u001b[82GThe\u001b[86G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m<head>\u